+# The Daily Grind account
+
+A responsive, static account UI. Open `/` or serve `index.html` through a static host with an `/account` fallback. No dependencies or build step are required.
+
+The default account is a **demo**: sample passkeys persist in localStorage, with rename, delete, add-sample, empty states, and cross-tab refresh. Demo operations never create or modify WebAuthn credentials. Other site navigation preserves the original site routes.
+
+## Connect authenticated account data
+
+The repository has no authentication or backend. A host application can opt into real account management by adding these elements to the document head:
+
+```html
+<meta name="passkey-api" content="/api/account/passkeys">
+<meta name="csrf-token" content="SERVER_GENERATED_TOKEN">
+```
+
+Implement these same-origin endpoints with session authentication, account ownership checks, and CSRF protection:
+
+- `GET /api/account/passkeys`: list the authenticated customer's passkeys.
+- `PATCH /api/account/passkeys/:id` with `{ "name": "My laptop" }`: validate and rename the owned credential (1–50 trimmed characters).
+- `DELETE /api/account/passkeys/:id`: revoke the owned credential on the server before returning success. Ensure a usable recovery/sign-in method remains according to your account policy.
+
+All successful responses return the full authoritative snapshot:
+
+```json
+{
+  "rpId": "coffee.example.com",
+  "userId": "BASE64URL_WEBAUTHN_USER_HANDLE",
+  "passkeys": [{
+    "id": "BASE64URL_CREDENTIAL_ID",
+    "name": "MacBook Pro",
+    "device": "laptop",
+    "provider": "iCloud Keychain",
+    "created": "Oct 12, 2026",
+    "lastUsed": "Today",
+    "current": true
+  }]
+}
+```
+
+Do not return demo records. API mode never falls back to sample data on an authentication or network failure. Registration is outside this management API; the sample-add button is hidden in API mode.
+
+Following a confirmed server deletion, `signalAllAcceptedCredentials` sends the complete remaining credential list to supported browser authenticators. Unsupported browsers and rejected signals show instructions to remove the saved passkey manually. A resolved signal confirms notification, not guaranteed deletion by every password manager. Renaming changes the site's friendly label only; the WebAuthn user-details signal does not rename individual credentials.
+
+Reference: [WebAuthn Signal API specification](https://www.w3.org/TR/webauthn/#dom-publickeycredential-signalallacceptedcredentials).
